        "question": "What is Langchain and how it is related with langgraph",
        "answer": "LangChain is a framework designed to connect large language models into structured workflows, enabling multi-step reasoning and automation. It is ideal for simpler, linear workflows, rapid prototyping, and extensive integrations, easily integrating with popular LLMs, external APIs, databases, and tools through its modular chain design.\n\nLangGraph is created by the LangChain team and extends LangChain's capabilities to support complex, stateful agent workflows. It is built on LangChain and is part of the same ecosystem. While LangChain excels at sequential pipelines, LangGraph handles complex, stateful workflows with loops, branches, and multiple agents. They are complementary tools, not competitors, providing a comprehensive solution for building sophisticated autonomous AI agents.",
